BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bassoonist Scott Pool & EK Duo
DTSTART:20261023T190000
DTEND:20261023T210000
DTSTAMP:20261022T155525Z
UID:109583ab6d75c7911a9282699771e1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Upstream Classical presents bassoonist Scott Pool & EK Duo per
 forming unusual and off-the-beaten path music for two bassoons and percuss
 ion. Folk\, pop & classical elements blend together in novel ways with wor
 ks by Louis Andriessen\, Billie Eilish and EK Duo's own Thomas Kozumplik\,
  who is featured on steel drum. EK Duo is a project of longtime Clogs' ban
 dmates\, percussionist Thomas Kozumplik and bassoonist Rachael Elliott. Sc
 ott Pool\, based in Corpus Christi\, is the Academy Director of the Talis 
 Music Festival & Academy in Sarajevo\, Bosnia and Herzegovina and has tour
 ed widely across the Americas\, Europe and Asia. EK Duo first performed wi
 th Scott in 2024 while touring Texas and are delighted to collaborate with
  him on his first shows in Vermont.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:York Street Meeting House\, 153 York St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bassoonist
 -scott-pool-ek-duo-25-09-2026-11-58-44
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buddhadeva by Akaina Ghosh
DTSTART:20261023T193000
DTEND:20261023T213000
DTSTAMP:20261022T155525Z
UID:12d0308968f319a6d9471acef420b4@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In Buddhadeva\, Akaina Ghosh creates a tender\, searching solo
  performance in conversation with the life and work of their great-grandfa
 ther\, the prolific Bengali writer and poet Buddhadeva Bose. Set along the
  banks of the Ganga River\, the piece moves through poetry\, memory\, love
 \, loss\, and translation. As Ghosh attempts to conjure a relationship wit
 h an ancestor known largely through scattered words and inherited fragment
 s\, they explore their own identity as a non-binary\, second-generation Am
 erican-Bengali artist. What is lost in translation? What can be recovered 
 from the pieces of a family’s past? Buddhadeva is an intimate meditation
  on language and lineage—an invitation to consider the people\, stories
 \, and silences that shape who we are. Next Stage Arts\n\nSources: Vermont
  Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/buddhadeva
 -by-akaina-ghosh-24-09-2026-12-57-10
END:VEVENT
