BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Vermont to Palestine: Building Global Solidarity
DTSTART:20261023T163000
DTEND:20261023T183000
DTSTAMP:20261022T155525Z
UID:79fb7f15454a47fae2bfb81950140e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Community groups will table and share examples of ways to get 
 involved in the solidarity work happening in Vermont and across the world.
  The panelists are: • Hamed Bakir\, a Palestinian American public health
  and environmental specialist and retired United Nations professional. Ham
 ed was raised in Ramallah\, Palestine\, with family roots in Jaffa. • Wa
 fic Faour\, a Palestinian American born in a refugee camp to parents who b
 ecame refugees in 1948. Wafic has lived in Vermont for 30+ years and is a 
 longtime organizer with Vermont Coalition for Palestinian Liberation\, a c
 ollaboration of Vermont organizations and residents working together for a
  free Palestine • Kate Paarlberg-Kvam\, a Vermont People’s Arms Embarg
 o member and activist with the International Solidarity Movement\, a Pales
 tinian-led organization focused on assisting the Palestinian cause in the 
 Israeli-Palestinian conflict. • Rory C\, co-director of the Peace & Just
 ice Center in Burlington\, a Vermont People’s Arms Embargo member\, and 
 an activist supporting Indigenous rights from Vermont to Palestine. The pa
 nel moderator is Max Schindler\, a UVM history graduate student focusing o
 n how Hebrew newspapers reported on Ottoman land law and a former journali
 st for Israeli TV and publications including The Jerusalem Post. Schindler
  volunteered for several months in Massafer Yatta\, collection of 19 Pales
 tinian hamlets\, some of which are under Israeli military demolition order
 s.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Dudley H. Davis Center\, Silver Maple Ballroom\, 590 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/from-vermo
 nt-to-palestine-building-global-solidarity-14-10-2026-14-13-24
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hollywood\, VT at the Latchis Theatre: LIVE Screenplay Reading of 
 The Trouble with Harry
DTSTART:20261023T190000
DTEND:20261023T213000
DTSTAMP:20261022T155525Z
UID:9223efd0a614336281f5ba8c2ac802@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that more than 70 years ago Alfred Hitchcock came
  to Vermont to film and premiere The Trouble with Harry — a darkly funny
  romantic comedy about a corpse\, a group of neighbors\, and the increasin
 gly complicated question of what to do with the body? This fall\, we're br
 inging Harry back two ways at the Latchis Theatre in Brattleboro. Friday\,
  October 23 — LIVE Screenplay Reading For one night only\, an all–Verm
 ont-connected cast takes on John Michael Hayes's screenplay in a largely u
 nrehearsed live reading featuring Tom Bodett (Wait Wait… Don't Tell Me!
 \, Motel 6)\, Myra Flynn (singer-songwriter\, journalist\, Homegoings)\, J
 eanine B. Frost (AFI alum\, Vermont writer/director/actor)\, and Chris Dor
 man (creator and star of Vermont Public's Mister Chris and Friends)\, with
  additional casting to be announced. Sunday\, November 8 — Film Screenin
 g + Community Conversation See Hitchcock's 1955 film on the big screen\, s
 tarring Shirley MacLaine (The Apartment\, Terms of Endearment)\, John Fors
 ythe (Dynasty\, Charlie's Angels)\, Edmund Gwenn (Miracle on 34th Street)
 \, Mildred Natwick (Barefoot in the Park)\, and Jerry Mathers (Leave It to
  Beaver)\, followed by a community conversation moderated by Vermont filmm
 aker Bess O'Brien\, Jeanine B. Frost and additional guests to be announced
 . Come for one event or join us for both — from page\, to stage\, to scr
 een and straight into your hearts!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/hollywood-
 vt-at-the-latchis-theatre-live-screenplay-reading-of-the-trouble-with-harr
 y-26-09-2026-17-08-34
END:VEVENT
