BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Oct. 23 | Hitchcock's 'The Trouble With Harry': Live Screenplay Re
 ading
DTSTART:20261023T190000
DTEND:20261023T220000
DTSTAMP:20261022T155525Z
UID:a6674b9069dd94b490b291c794b70e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:More than 70 years after Alfred Hitchcock came to Vermont to m
 ake The Trouble with Harry\, Hollywood\, VT revisits the wonderfully stran
 ge dark comedy in two ways: first\, a one-night-only\, largely unrehearsed
  live reading of John Michael Hayes’s screenplay with a Vermont-connecte
 d cast\; then\, a screening of Hitchcock’s 1955 film followed by a commu
 nity conversation. A dead man is discovered on a Vermont hillside\, and a 
 group of neighbors become entangled in the increasingly complicated questi
 on of what to do with the body. Oct. 23 cast: Tom Bodett (NPR’s Wait Wai
 t… Don’t Tell Me!\, Motel 6)\, Myra Flynn (Vermont singer-songwriter\,
  journalist and recent This American Life contributor)\, Jeanine B. Frost 
 (AFI graduate\, Vermont writer\, director and actor)\, and Chris Dorman (M
 usician\, child educator and creator and star of Mister Chris and Friends)
 \, with additional casting to be announced.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/oct-23-hit
 chcocks-the-trouble-with-harry-live-screenplay-reading-29-09-2026-09-58-46
END:VEVENT
